+- **feat(home):** the home Provider Topology now shows a logo-only router core with an electric "kame beam" on active links, a live **Recent Requests** panel (polls `/api/usage/call-logs` every ~3s, gated by the topology appearance toggle + page visibility), a ring that grows with the provider count so many providers no longer overlap, and only surfaces providers with an enabled connection — untested/failing connections no longer clutter the map. Nodes are ordered by creation time, so adding a provider appends it instead of pushing the existing map around, and a compatible node without a custom `icon_url` now renders the same bundled logo the providers page shows instead of a generic glyph. The error counter and the red edges reflect **every** currently-failing provider (`/api/provider-metrics` gained `topology.errorProviders`); previously only the most recent failure was reported, so a second failure silently cleared the first. All topology animations honour `prefers-reduced-motion` ([#8450](https://github.com/diegosouzapw/OmniRoute/pull/8450)) — thanks @nguyenha935
